TOPIC 20 - Index, View, Transaction - Advanced For Senior
================================================================
CONCEPT - 3 Parts:

PART A - INDEX - Makes Search Fast
Index is like index in book. Without index, PostgreSQL checks 1 Lakh rows one by one. With index, it jumps directly.
COMMAND:
CREATE INDEX index_name ON table(column);

EXAMPLE:
CREATE INDEX idx_cibil ON loan_table(cibil);

-- Now this query will be fast:
SELECT * FROM loan_table WHERE cibil = 750;

PROJECT USE: When table has 1 Lakh rows, index makes search fast for FastAPI.

PART B - VIEW - Saved Query, Virtual Table
View is saved SELECT query. You save query once, use again like table.

COMMAND:
CREATE VIEW view_name AS SELECT ...;

EXAMPLE:
CREATE VIEW high_cibil AS SELECT * FROM loan_table WHERE cibil > 700;

-- Now use view like table:
SELECT * FROM high_cibil;

OUTPUT:
Hyarel 750, Sneha 720

PROJECT USE: Save high CIBIL customers as view, dashboard uses view directly.

PART C - TRANSACTION - All Or Nothing
Transaction = Group of queries. Either all succeed, or none succeed.
BEGIN = Start, COMMIT = Save, ROLLBACK = Cancel.

COMMAND:
BEGIN;
Query1;
Query2;
COMMIT; -- or ROLLBACK;

EXAMPLE:
-- Transfer money - Debit from Hyarel, Credit to Priya - Both must happen
BEGIN;
UPDATE loan_table SET salary = salary - 10000 WHERE name = 'Hyarel';
UPDATE loan_table SET salary = salary + 10000 WHERE name = 'Priya';
COMMIT;

If second query fails, do ROLLBACK, first query also cancelled. Money safe.

PROJECT USE: Money transfer, payment - Must be all or nothing.

INTERVIEW ANSWER:
Index makes search fast, View is saved query, Transaction is all or nothing.

